=====

Use this action when users ask about revenue decline, drop-offs, or customers ordering less between any two time periods.

WHEN TO USE:
- "Which customers had declining revenue in Q1?"
- "Show revenue drop between [period] and [period]"
- "Customers with less orders this quarter"
- "Who stopped ordering or reduced purchases?"
- "Revenue drop-off analysis"
- "Compare revenue between [timeframe]"

HOW TO USE:
1. Parse the user's query to identify the two time periods they want to compare
2. Convert periods to exact dates:
   - Q1: January 1 - March 31
   - Q2: April 1 - June 30
   - Q3: July 1 - September 30
   - Q4: October 1 - December 31
   - "Last 6 months": Calculate 6 months back from today
   - "This year vs last year": Calculate full year dates

3. Always compare OLDER period first (period1) vs NEWER period (period2)
   Example: "Q1 revenue drop" means Q4 2024 (period1) → Q1 2025 (period2)

4. If user doesn't specify periods, leave dates EMPTY to auto-compare current vs previous quarter

DATE PARAMETER EXAMPLES:
Query: "declining revenue in Q1 2025"
→ period1Start: 2024-10-01, period1End: 2024-12-31 (Q4 2024)
→ period2Start: 2025-01-01, period2End: 2025-03-31 (Q1 2025)

Query: "revenue drop last 3 months"
→ Calculate: 3 months ago to today vs 6-3 months ago

Query: "customers ordering less this quarter"
→ Leave all dates empty (action will auto-calculate)

IMPORTANT:
- Always specify ALL 4 dates when user mentions specific periods
- Leave ALL dates empty only when user says "current" or "this quarter" without specifics
- Period 1 should always be the EARLIER/BASELINE period
- Period 2 should always be the LATER/COMPARISON period
